WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
- Do you dream about playing

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.963
Apex Raid of Shadows in your sleep?

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.875
- Apex Raid of Shadows?

00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:08.196
(laughing loudly)

00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:10.786
- Do you try and be a boomer on purpose?

00:00:10.786 --> 00:00:12.730
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.160
- What's up friends and Chris?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.750
Welcome back to another episode
of the Trash Taste Podcast.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.110
I'm the boy,

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.650
and I'm with the boys and Chris.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.320
- And what is going on
with your head, Chris?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.260
- Well, I won worst drip,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.093
right?

00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:25.926
- Laziest drip.

00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:26.759
- Laziest drip--
- Laziest drip.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:27.592
- Whatever it is, when I won though,

00:00:27.592 --> 00:00:28.550
I thought it was something coffee, right?

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.430
Like, 'cause I use an espresso machine,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.920
I thought the laziest drip coffee,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.297
and espresso.

00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:35.150
(laughs loudly)
So I was like, oh,

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.540
that's bad, but it's not too bad.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.847
Then I discovered it was about clothes.

00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:38.852
(Garnt laughing loudly)

00:00:38.852 --> 00:00:39.685
And, you know,

00:00:39.685 --> 00:00:42.860
I'm like the king of
fashion as we all know.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.590
- So you won laziest drip,

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.270
and you somehow came with even worse drip?

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.500
- So why the hat, why the hat?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.333
Is that in response?

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:50.166
- That's what I want to know.

00:00:50.166 --> 00:00:51.620
- This is the standard of drip.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.040
- You look like you just
walked out from the nineties.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.930
- Wait, what does his hat say?

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.100
- It says jumping.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.715
- Jumping, pounding the rock.

00:00:59.715 --> 00:01:01.530
- Things I stand for.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:05.037
But I wanna win best drip or
whatever it's called next year,

00:01:05.037 --> 00:01:07.745
and this is the first step
to making that happen so.

00:01:07.745 --> 00:01:09.420
- People probably clicked on this video

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.390
on the thumbnail of this, Chris.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.223
And they're probably like,

00:01:12.223 --> 00:01:13.113
What happened to Chris?

00:01:13.113 --> 00:01:15.310
- It's a new Chris for a new year.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.000
But where are we, what is this place?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:17.833
- Oh yeah!

00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:20.580
So you're the first
guest for the new studio.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.590
How do you find it?

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.879
- You guys used to record
in a broom cupboard.

00:01:23.879 --> 00:01:24.920
A well decorated broom cupboard,

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.520
but a broom cupboard nonetheless.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.320
But this is like what can only be

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.270
described as a Bond's villains' lair.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.550
(all laughing loudly)

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.660
I got to the building outside,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.278
it's all like tinted windows,

00:01:35.278 --> 00:01:37.910
a security team I have
to get past to get in.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.340
And I'm like, what is this?

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.440
- You came with the Uber driver,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.847
or the Uber Eats driver, right?.

00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:42.830
- The only way I got into this building,

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.530
nobody told me the code or anything.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.580
And there was like an Uber guy,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.979
he was equally confused,

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:49.070
and we sort of made a team effort.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.915
Like he got me through the
first door, the security door,

00:01:51.915 --> 00:01:53.842
and then I got him through this door.

00:01:53.842 --> 00:01:55.690
It's sort of a team tag,

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.890
team effort to get in
this ridiculous building.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:58.723
It is massive.

00:01:58.723 --> 00:02:00.610
We could have a game of cricket in here.

00:02:02.442 --> 00:02:04.553
- That's the most British
thing you've ever said.

00:02:04.553 --> 00:02:05.497
- It is cool, it is quite cool.

00:02:05.497 --> 00:02:07.267
I feel really out of my depth now.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.820
- But yeah, we got Chris
back for the third time.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.954
- He wanted to assert
dominance as soon as he

00:02:11.954 --> 00:02:13.930
found out that we got a new studio.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.460
- So Chris is like the first guest

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.400
we've ever had on the show--

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.740
- Literally the second episode
in the new studio, right?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.573
Yeah.

00:02:22.573 --> 00:02:23.406
- Yeah, the second
episode in the new studio.

00:02:23.406 --> 00:02:26.070
But Chris was not only
our first guest ever,

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.870
but he was the first guest of this year,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.048
and now he's the first
guest of the new studio.

00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:31.600
Just knocking out all the firsts.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.120
- And I won the best
guest and the best drip,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.020
or the worst drip-

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.853
- Laziest drip.

00:02:35.853 --> 00:02:36.967
- Yeah, congratulations about that.

00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:39.078
We do have something for you.

00:02:39.078 --> 00:02:41.545
- That's the reason I'm here.

00:02:41.545 --> 00:02:43.220
I didn't come here to look enviously

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.594
at your massive studio space,

00:02:44.594 --> 00:02:46.310
'cause I record in a wardrobe.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.800
My recording pad is in a wardrobe,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.840
and I came here to get an award.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.560
A physical, tangible,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.764
monetary award.

00:02:52.764 --> 00:02:53.653
(all laughing quickly)

00:02:53.653 --> 00:02:57.193
- Monetary, something that is worthwhile.

00:02:58.055 --> 00:02:58.990
- Go on, Ashley.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.147
Ashley's got it.

00:03:00.147 --> 00:03:00.980
- Is there actually an award?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:01.813
Is it actually an award?

00:03:01.813 --> 00:03:03.947
- I knew that this was
what we had to get you.

00:03:03.947 --> 00:03:05.351
- Before you open it,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.922
do you want to give a speech
or something like that?

00:03:06.922 --> 00:03:07.755
- Yeah, a little acceptance.

00:03:07.755 --> 00:03:08.588
- Yeah, go on.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.451
A little acceptance speech.

00:03:09.451 --> 00:03:11.373
- So everyone that voted me
for the best guest, thank you.

00:03:11.373 --> 00:03:12.610
You are my favorites.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.260
Everyone that voted
worst drip, I hate you.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.010
(all laughing loudly)

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.120
You're wrong,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.748
and I'm gonna prove you
wrong for the next year.

00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:24.862
- This is an award that
all three of us were like,

00:03:24.862 --> 00:03:25.695
you know--

00:03:25.695 --> 00:03:26.528
- Why are you laughing?

00:03:27.486 --> 00:03:28.598
It's an award!

00:03:28.598 --> 00:03:31.680
- It is a bomb in there,
it's gonna blow up.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.737
- The tape doesn't help.

00:03:33.737 --> 00:03:35.097
- Open your prize up.

00:03:35.097 --> 00:03:36.050
- It looks like one of those special bombs

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.439
that only kills the
person who's holding it.

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:39.019
(laughs quickly)

00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:40.928
- How do you know about that?

00:03:40.928 --> 00:03:43.220
- We thought this would
be perfect for you.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.895
- It's even better than a bomb, Chris.

00:03:44.895 --> 00:03:45.728
- Yeah, when we thought about award.

00:03:45.728 --> 00:03:46.561
I was like, guys,

00:03:46.561 --> 00:03:48.470
I know exactly what we need to get Chris.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.770
- Is it actually good?
- Yeah, I'd love it.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.693
I think it's the best thing ever--

00:03:51.693 --> 00:03:52.908
- It's brilliant, it's brilliant.

00:03:52.908 --> 00:03:55.177
- Just rip it open, just rip it open.

00:03:55.177 --> 00:03:56.562
- I'm doing it Japanese style--

00:03:56.562 --> 00:03:57.395
- No, fucking rip it.

00:03:57.395 --> 00:03:58.228
Rip it open.

00:03:58.228 --> 00:04:00.690
- In Japan they're kind of
very intricate, aren't they?

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.073
- [Boys] Yeah.

00:04:02.073 --> 00:04:04.150
- Hold it to the camera first.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:04.983
Hold it to the camera first.

00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:07.894
- So it's some sort of
image, is it the right way?

00:04:07.894 --> 00:04:10.830
- [Garnt] Somehow he got it
the right way first time.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.180
- Everyone is laughing.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.220
Everyone behind the camera is laughing--

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.053
- And ready?

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.044
Three, two,
one!

00:04:16.044 --> 00:04:18.877
(laughing loudly)

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.160
You'll forever have that immortalized now.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.050
- Who drew this?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.160
I'm coming for you.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.803
Who did this?

00:04:31.803 --> 00:04:34.590
I'm gonna use the full
force of the Abroad in Japan

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.640
media empire to find the
person that drew this,

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.780
and bring them to justice.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.084
What is it?

00:04:39.084 --> 00:04:42.000
So this is like a manga?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.370
- [Joey] So this is a
webtoon that one of our

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.350
fans was making about Trash Taste.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.170
- And he's characterized all of us,

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.310
and I've got to say,

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.143
I mean, like.

00:04:49.143 --> 00:04:50.705
(laughs quickly)

00:04:50.705 --> 00:04:52.847
- I look like a fucking balloon.

00:04:52.847 --> 00:04:53.930
What is that?

00:04:54.791 --> 00:04:56.267
So I saw this on Twitter earlier.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:57.100
Oh, Chris,

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.769
you're in the Trash Taste gang.

00:04:58.769 --> 00:04:59.602
I was like, oh,

00:04:59.602 --> 00:05:00.560
that's great, I'm in a manga.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.454
And then I clicked
through and it was this,

00:05:02.454 --> 00:05:03.480
and I was like, which one am I?

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.390
Am I, oh.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:05.710
I'm the fat one.

00:05:07.821 --> 00:05:09.880
- I remember the message you gave me too,

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.560
because you sent me a screenshot of this,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.160
and after it, it just said,

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.121
you fucking what?

00:05:14.121 --> 00:05:15.570
(laughs quickly)

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:20.088
- I mean, it does look like me
if we remove the lower half.

00:05:20.088 --> 00:05:22.050
- It does look shockingly like you.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.750
I did ask when we got this frame made,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.870
like, can we get a Kim
Jong Un sized picture?

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.140
- Yeah, a massive one that
you can put on the wall,

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.770
and we just pray to every morning--

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.543
- Taking out of the bullet
trade and back to center.

00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:33.821
(all laughing quickly)

00:05:33.821 --> 00:05:34.810
- Just hold it.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.270
- This character, it's not
even called Chris or Abroad.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.812
- It's called Bigmouth, Fatman.

00:05:39.812 --> 00:05:41.729
- Bigmouth.
- Fatmouth.

00:05:43.321 --> 00:05:44.688
- Bigmouth.

00:05:44.688 --> 00:05:45.521
- I think it's shocking.

00:05:45.521 --> 00:05:48.530
- I think in the webtoon
we all have special powers

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.315
that are kind of synonymous
to our personalities.

00:05:51.315 --> 00:05:52.520
(laughs quickly)

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.824
You got it.

00:05:54.824 --> 00:05:57.899
- I really hope this character
has a redemption arc.

00:05:57.899 --> 00:05:59.870
Where he gets thin, he saves the world,

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.800
he gets the girl, 'cause
that's just an atrocity.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.291
But it does look cool.

00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:05.374
I do like it.

00:06:05.374 --> 00:06:06.401
- The poor artist who made this.

00:06:06.401 --> 00:06:07.520
- I'll put that in a very special place

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.329
in my apartment for everyone to see it.

00:06:09.329 --> 00:06:10.380
- Is it gonna go?

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:11.930
- Yeah, this better be on the set.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.773
- Yeah, I'll think about it.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.440
(laughs quickly)

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.080
Thank you, it's the thought that counts.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.749
- Someone's put a lot of effort into that,

00:06:19.749 --> 00:06:20.700
and, I mean--

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.140
- It's a winning prize.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.442
- Is it?

00:06:24.442 --> 00:06:26.060
I thought it would be a
gold bar or something.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.120
- Why would we give you a gold bullion?

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.147
- This is Trash Taste!

00:06:29.147 --> 00:06:30.680
- Something I could sell off when

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.181
my channel goes down the toilet.

00:06:32.181 --> 00:06:33.014
I can be like, oh,

00:06:33.014 --> 00:06:33.847
I've got the Trash Taste prize.

00:06:33.847 --> 00:06:34.960
I can sell that off.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.412
That's like worth nothing, but it's good.

00:06:37.412 --> 00:06:38.280
It's good I think--

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.118
- How dare you.
- Thank you very much.

00:06:40.118 --> 00:06:42.590
- We put a lot of love
and effort into this.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.385
- This can live on the
table for this episode.

00:06:45.385 --> 00:06:46.956
- Yeah, for this episode.
- Fantastic.

00:06:46.956 --> 00:06:47.789
- On the table. (laughs quickly)

00:06:47.789 --> 00:06:50.760
- Is there more manga of this coming out?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:51.855
- I think so.

00:06:51.855 --> 00:06:53.830
- This was like two or three months ago.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.440
- I think the guy is making a new

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.850
chapter every week or two weeks,

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.683
something like that?

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.572
- Redemption arc, redemption arc.

00:06:58.572 --> 00:06:59.420
- Don't give him the redemption arc.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.670
- It takes time to draw things, Chris.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.517
- Especially when
they're that fucking big.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.790
That's like 70% of the image is just me.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.743
Awful, but it's a great drawing--

00:07:10.743 --> 00:07:12.831
- Isn't it great you're like
the center of attention?

00:07:12.831 --> 00:07:13.664
- Exactly, you're right in the middle.

00:07:13.664 --> 00:07:15.220
You're pushing away your competition.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:17.270
- Redemption arc, and I'll be very happy.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.020
Let's get fit or something.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.730
- The next one just has to be like this,

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.981
but with this hat on him.

00:07:22.981 --> 00:07:24.240
- Fatmouth, brilliant.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.160
- Fatmouth with a cap.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.630
- Yeah, is that hat something
you'd normally wear,

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.690
Chris, or it it something you just wear?

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:30.523
- I've never seen you wear a hat.

00:07:30.523 --> 00:07:32.400
- I've got a collection of 100 Yen hats.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.667
This was 100 Yen, right?

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:36.299
'Cause in Japan you get
a lot of hats that just,

00:07:36.299 --> 00:07:38.916
(laughs loudly)

00:07:38.916 --> 00:07:41.011
They've got some really
obscure English ones.

00:07:41.011 --> 00:07:43.310
This is actually like a
basketball saying, right?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.336
- Is it?

00:07:44.336 --> 00:07:45.495
- I think it's something, you know,

00:07:45.495 --> 00:07:46.520
putting the ball through the hoop.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.570
- Probably, maybe.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.080
- Only one of my friends knew that,

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.670
and he's like a top basketball guy.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.503
He's like--

00:07:51.503 --> 00:07:52.336
- It just sounds like you want to have

00:07:52.336 --> 00:07:53.169
sex with Dwayne the Rock Johnson.

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:54.510
- It does a bit, it does a bit.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.830
But out of context it's
just so bizarre, isn't it?

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.280
So I have a collection of these

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.894
sort of tacky hats in my apartment.

00:07:59.894 --> 00:08:01.854
Now I'm actually wearing one.

00:08:01.854 --> 00:08:04.743
- So you have a collection of tacky hats,

00:08:04.743 --> 00:08:06.477
and you're like, how dare
you give me laziest drip?

00:08:06.477 --> 00:08:07.960
- Let me wear this tacky hat.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.300
- Yeah, let me wear this hundred Yen hat.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.810
- It does give off very much dad energy.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:12.643
- Yeah!

00:08:12.643 --> 00:08:15.338
- I'm pretty sure my dad has
worn the same hat before.

00:08:15.338 --> 00:08:16.357
(laughs quietly)

00:08:16.357 --> 00:08:19.580
- I don't know how I feel about that part.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.420
I'll take it, I like the hat.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.698
Let's get best drip.

00:08:22.698 --> 00:08:23.999
What's is it?

00:08:23.999 --> 00:08:25.635
- Best drip, best drip.

00:08:25.635 --> 00:08:26.820
Best drip, yeah.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.840
- Where does the word drip
come from in that context?

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.802
- I don't know.
- I actually don't know.

00:08:30.802 --> 00:08:32.540
- It became a meme,

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:34.730
and I didn't know what it meant initially.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.563
But, I don't know,

00:08:35.563 --> 00:08:37.390
it's a word where you hear it once,

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.270
and you hear the word drip,

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.103
and for some reason, for me,

00:08:39.103 --> 00:08:40.290
it just made sense.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.396
- Like bussin'.

00:08:41.396 --> 00:08:42.640
- Bussin' doesn't make sense.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.071
- You're bussin'?
- Bussin'.

00:08:44.071 --> 00:08:45.766
- Man, that shit's bussin'.

00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:47.460
- What is this?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.338
I feel really old now.

00:08:49.338 --> 00:08:51.093
I'm 31, I'm out of the loop here.

00:08:51.093 --> 00:08:52.610
- Like when something's just great.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:53.600
- Yeah, so when something's really good,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:54.433
you go, damn,

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.266
that's bussin'.

00:08:55.266 --> 00:08:56.490
- I still get uncomfortable
when people use the word sick.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.600
Like oh, that's sick.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.600
'Cause I've just got--

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.798
- I use the word sick.

00:08:59.798 --> 00:09:01.376
- You just insulted all of Australia.

00:09:01.376 --> 00:09:03.600
- I've got quite a visual sort of imagery.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.270
When I hear a word, I picture it.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.210
Every time I hear sick,

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.123
I picture someone literally
being sick all over the table.

00:09:08.123 --> 00:09:09.160
(all laughing loudly)

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.943
That's not sick, that's horrible.

00:09:12.286 --> 00:09:14.060
You know, I'm older than you.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.029
How old are you?

00:09:15.029 --> 00:09:15.862
- Same age as Garnt.

00:09:15.862 --> 00:09:17.159
- Yeah, same age as Garnt--
- Yeah, same age as me.

00:09:17.159 --> 00:09:18.138
- But Garnt's youthful.

00:09:18.138 --> 00:09:20.233
(laughs loudly)

00:09:20.233 --> 00:09:21.887
You look like you're in your 20's,

00:09:21.887 --> 00:09:24.586
I look like I'm 47 or something?

00:09:24.586 --> 00:09:25.496
- Especially with the hat.

00:09:25.496 --> 00:09:26.700
- Especially with the hat.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.900
This is like my bridge
to the youth of time.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.560
- What we need to get you is a skateboard.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.830
Have you seen that Steve Buscemi

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.091
image where he's just like,

00:09:34.091 --> 00:09:35.272
hello, fellow children.

00:09:35.272 --> 00:09:37.143
(laughs loudly)

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.974
- It's all part of my plan.

00:09:38.974 --> 00:09:41.260
Get with the youth, get
the demographic bigger.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.000
- It's like he's trying to
sneak into a high school.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:43.833
- Yeah, right?

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:45.963
Hello, fellow kids.

00:09:47.028 --> 00:09:48.440
Oh my God.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.810
- So what's the plan for today?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.094
Usually when I come here--

00:09:51.094 --> 00:09:52.500
- We don't do that here.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.140
- We'll just chat shit like usual, right?

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.015
- Excellent.

00:09:55.015 --> 00:09:56.039
- What you been up to, Chris?

00:09:56.039 --> 00:09:56.872
- Yeah, what have you been up to?

00:09:56.872 --> 00:09:58.440
Why you in Tokyo again?

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.273
- Oh, what have I been doing.

00:09:59.273 --> 00:10:02.201
I filmed a building, that's about it.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.470
- A single building?

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:04.810
- Well, I came down here to win my award,

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:08.203
and starting to worry that
that was money not well spent.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.294
- You literally spent like
100 bucks to come down--

00:10:13.294 --> 00:10:15.143
- It's like a four hour
round trip to get here,

00:10:15.143 --> 00:10:17.100
and that's just to be insulted

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.019
on the world's biggest podcast.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.153
Brilliant.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.172
Was it worth it?

00:10:22.172 --> 00:10:23.005
You decide.

00:10:23.005 --> 00:10:24.040
- A lot of people die for that experience.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.290
- You also did a Journey Across Japan.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.220
- Yeah, it's been going well.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:29.540
We've got like a top 15 iTunes hit.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:30.959
- I can't fucking believe that.

00:10:30.959 --> 00:10:32.100
- I don't know how that--

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.880
- I spent so much of my
time just off camera,

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.140
you know, making my own music,

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:37.480
and putting my heart and soul into it,

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:41.110
and the most successful piece
of music I've ever written

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.453
I wrote in seven hours in a car.

00:10:43.453 --> 00:10:44.609
- The world is often a cruel fixture.

00:10:44.609 --> 00:10:46.030
- You know what, I'll take the award.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:46.863
It's all right.

00:10:46.863 --> 00:10:48.780
- Yeah, so for those
who aren't in the know,

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:49.723
what's the story behind that?

00:10:49.723 --> 00:10:52.010
- We had a challenge where
we had to do a rap song.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.940
Soul Angelic Japan, this travel series,

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:54.830
we get a challenge everyday,

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.830
and the challenge was
produce a rap song in a day.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.310
And we found ourselves a volcano,

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.143
and that became--

00:11:01.143 --> 00:11:02.270
- We had to rap about our day, right?

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.810
- Yeah, and we're on the top
of Japan's biggest volcano,

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.797
Mount Aso, and that became it.

00:11:06.797 --> 00:11:08.180
And Natsky said something like, whoa,

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.160
too much volcano!

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:09.993
We're like, yeah,

00:11:09.993 --> 00:11:11.060
it is, isn't it?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:11.893
That's the rap.

00:11:11.893 --> 00:11:13.980
- Say that over and over again, say that.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.570
- I very cleverly didn't put
myself in the rap or the video,

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.403
so that's good.

00:11:18.403 --> 00:11:21.270
Just you and Natsky that took the credit.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:23.330
But yeah, it turned out really well.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.280
- Yeah.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.421
- I put it on iTunes, right?

00:11:25.421 --> 00:11:28.474
It costs like $19 to put a song on iTunes,

00:11:28.474 --> 00:11:30.560
and it takes a few weeks.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.720
It's very simple,

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.610
but whilst I did that I shouted it out,

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:34.920
and it started to go up.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.020
Someone sent me a link saying, oh,

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:39.522
you're in the top 25
alternative songs on iTunes.

00:11:39.522 --> 00:11:40.355
I was kind of like--

00:11:40.355 --> 00:11:41.470
- Alternative songs?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.303
- For that week, right?

00:11:42.303 --> 00:11:43.136
So it's like, oh,

00:11:43.136 --> 00:11:43.969
okay, you know,

00:11:43.969 --> 00:11:45.630
it's probably because of
the initial push on Twitter.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.515
- Yeah, yeah.

00:11:46.515 --> 00:11:49.150
- But then it just, it just kept going.

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:50.000
It just kept climbing.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.850
- Yeah, once I shouted
out that we're on iTunes,

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.930
it created this sort of
self-propelling sort of cycle.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.421
People funded it more, bought it more,

00:11:55.421 --> 00:11:57.310
and it went up and up until it got to,

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.020
I think number 14 on the
iTunes singles chart worldwide.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:03.180
- These poor people who bought this song.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.356
It's terrible.

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:06.520
It is worryingly catchy.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.353
- It is quite addictive,

00:12:07.353 --> 00:12:09.934
The song hook with Natsky
and 'too much volcano'--

00:12:09.934 --> 00:12:10.767
- Yeah, the ASO,

00:12:10.767 --> 00:12:11.600
too much volcano.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.270
- It works, it works.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.756
So I don't know how much it sold.

00:12:14.756 --> 00:12:16.290
- I don't know either.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:18.200
I'm still waiting for my
royalties to be honest.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.192
- Well, yeah.

00:12:19.192 --> 00:12:21.430
I wasn't going to split
it with Natsky and Joey

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:24.074
because I thought it would make like $100,

00:12:24.074 --> 00:12:25.510
oh, I'll use that to buy a coffee,

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.498
or a new hat, 10 hats.

00:12:27.498 --> 00:12:29.184
That's like 1000 hats?

00:12:29.184 --> 00:12:30.173
- That's like 1000 hats, damn!

00:12:30.173 --> 00:12:32.260
- 1000 hats!
- The drip game.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.343
- But because probably around
10,000 people bought it,

00:12:36.251 --> 00:12:37.084
that's a bit more money,

00:12:37.084 --> 00:12:38.880
and it makes sense to split that

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.270
with you and Natsky I think.

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.370
- Just pocket it, just be like--

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.203
- I'll just lie, I'll be like,

00:12:42.203 --> 00:12:43.938
oh, I only sold 100 copies.

00:12:43.938 --> 00:12:46.360
- You're mirroring the music industry,

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.789
where the guy behind
it takes all the money.

00:12:48.789 --> 00:12:51.372
- Producer takes all the money.

00:12:52.208 --> 00:12:53.090
- But I don't know.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:54.930
Unfortunately it takes about three months

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.040
for iTunes to tell you how well it's done,

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.690
so one day in September I'll
be sitting in a room depressed

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.640
and then I'll get a little
letter from iTunes like,

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.690
by the way, you've gone platinum!

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:04.523
Oh wow, platinum.

00:13:04.523 --> 00:13:06.100
I don't know what that is, but good.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:06.933
So we'll see, but yeah.

00:13:06.933 --> 00:13:09.233
- It's going on LinkedIn,
top selling artist--

00:13:09.233 --> 00:13:10.420
- It's going on the LinkedIn, top 14.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.760
- I think platinum means
one million copies sold.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:13.849
- [All] Yeah.

00:13:13.849 --> 00:13:15.820
- But getting there, right?

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:18.520
When you quitting YouTube and
starting your music career?

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.100
- Do we have permission to play
a small clip on the podcast?

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.240
- Copyright strike time.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.710
- Yeah, exactly!

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.587
- It's the only song that's not copyright.

00:13:25.587 --> 00:13:26.907
(laughs quickly)

00:13:26.907 --> 00:13:29.233
Use it to your advantage,
put it everywhere.

00:13:30.262 --> 00:13:31.147
Get those sales up.

00:13:31.147 --> 00:13:33.172
♪ Now we're chilling at
the peak of the volcano ♪

00:13:33.172 --> 00:13:35.369
♪ It looks kinda bleak
but it's okay though ♪

00:13:35.369 --> 00:13:36.228
♪ I'm with the bros ♪

00:13:36.228 --> 00:13:37.729
♪ Surrounded by the sulfur clouds ♪

00:13:37.729 --> 00:13:40.414
♪ So brace yourselves 'cause
it's about to get loud ♪

00:13:40.414 --> 00:13:42.713
♪ A-S-O ♪

00:13:42.713 --> 00:13:45.227
♪ Too much volcano ♪

00:13:45.227 --> 00:13:46.945
♪ No volcano ♪

00:13:46.945 --> 00:13:48.320
- Can't wait for you to
take this episode down

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:51.121
and claim on the entire ad revenue.

00:13:51.121 --> 00:13:52.320
- Just gonna all the ad--

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:56.340
- For this, yes I will.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.030
Take all the revenue.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.220
- You use my song, and you defamed me.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.310
(laughs loudly)

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:03.166
But there you go.

00:14:03.166 --> 00:14:04.720
It's that easy to get an iTunes
hit, ladies and gentlemen.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.710
- Yeah, apparently.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.650
Apparently.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.860
- If you have an influence online,

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:11.013
just beg your underlings to go and buy it.

00:14:11.013 --> 00:14:11.908
- Pretty much, pretty much.

00:14:11.908 --> 00:14:13.410
- Put Natsky in a song and it's

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.480
guaranteed to get on iTunes, you know?

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.313
- We're happy about that.

00:14:16.313 --> 00:14:18.700
- How was the overall journey
of Journey Across Japan,

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.660
which is an annual YouTube
series at this point?

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.105
- I don't know, I guess so.

00:14:23.105 --> 00:14:23.950
I thought all right, wasn't it?

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.011
- I guess it's annual, yeah.

00:14:25.011 --> 00:14:26.433
- Did you enjoy it?
- Yeah, it was really good.

00:14:26.433 --> 00:14:27.266
- Has it been doing well?

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:28.198
- I was there for the whole time.

00:14:28.198 --> 00:14:29.031
- I did enjoy it but,

00:14:29.031 --> 00:14:29.864
like, you know,

00:14:29.864 --> 00:14:31.590
'cause I'm always running
around filming and producing,

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.110
so it takes a lot of
stress because you got

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:35.110
to think everyday how's this gonna work.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:38.406
I nearly died on a horse, and in a plane.

00:14:38.406 --> 00:14:40.420
- In those videos when you say,

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.253
oh, it's one day,

00:14:41.253 --> 00:14:42.510
is it actually one day?

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:43.410
- For the most part--

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:44.243
- Yeah.
- Yeah, no.

00:14:44.243 --> 00:14:45.076
For the most part it was.

00:14:45.076 --> 00:14:47.202
- Because I feel like
there's way too much stuff.

00:14:47.202 --> 00:14:48.710
- It's extremely hectic.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:51.120
- What time are you
waking up, like 6:00 AM?

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.707
- Some days, yeah.

00:14:52.707 --> 00:14:53.540
- Oh my God.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.180
- And we're filming till
maybe like 10:00 or 11:00 PM.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:56.797
- It's relentless, it's a really crazy--

00:14:56.797 --> 00:14:58.647
- What's the crew behind that?

00:14:58.647 --> 00:14:59.963
- So it's Joey, myself,

00:14:59.963 --> 00:15:03.020
Natsky, and then we had a guy called Norm,

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.440
Tokyo Lens, and my friend Ian,

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.800
who's producing.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:09.430
And so it kind of works,
it's a pretty small team.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.263
- That's very small.

00:15:10.263 --> 00:15:12.210
I mean, we had that kind of team

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.230
for the Trash Taste Specials,

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.790
and even we were stretched to the

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:17.530
absolute limit with what we can do,

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.730
and just some of the stuff you're

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.011
able to do is fucking incredible.

00:15:20.011 --> 00:15:20.940
- It's honestly all thanks to just

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.320
Chris's insane organizational skills.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.220
Like he just has everything,

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.053
being like, all right--

00:15:25.053 --> 00:15:25.886
- Yeah, we don't have that.

00:15:25.886 --> 00:15:26.719
We don't.

00:15:26.719 --> 00:15:28.560
- At X time we're gonna
go here until here,

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.952
and then doing this after this,

00:15:29.952 --> 00:15:30.785
and then, oh,

00:15:30.785 --> 00:15:31.618
the weather's shit,

00:15:31.618 --> 00:15:32.540
maybe we should put this in front of this,

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.440
and me and Natsky just kind
of chilling in the back like,

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.273
all right,

00:15:35.273 --> 00:15:36.130
yeah, Chris.

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:37.120
- I somehow doubt Natsky's

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.870
too concerned with the scheduling.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:39.715
- Oh, he loved it.

00:15:39.715 --> 00:15:40.548
It was his holiday.

00:15:40.548 --> 00:15:41.381
He doesn't get to do anything really.

00:15:41.381 --> 00:15:43.520
He's like riding fucking horses,

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:45.210
he's going on a volcano dancing.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.474
- He literally had so much fun, yeah.

00:15:47.474 --> 00:15:48.873
- He's like seeing a cat, he loved it.

00:15:48.873 --> 00:15:50.377
It was the best trip of his life.

00:15:50.377 --> 00:15:52.480
Best holiday of his lifetime really.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.313
- Probably.

00:15:53.313 --> 00:15:54.146
- I love how you didn't,

00:15:54.146 --> 00:15:57.120
so in one of the episodes you
went to a cave or something?

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.260
And Chris just didn't go in the cave?

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:00.093
- Yeah, no.

00:16:00.093 --> 00:16:00.926
- Would you have gone in?

00:16:00.926 --> 00:16:01.759
- I would have gone in the cave

00:16:01.759 --> 00:16:02.970
I would have gone in.
- Bollocks.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:03.803
- Take me there, I will go in the cave.

00:16:03.803 --> 00:16:05.210
- It was such a humiliating day,

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.890
day three, Journey Across Japan.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.220
We went in the smallest
Torii gate in Japan.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:10.053
- Yeah, you almost got stuck.

00:16:10.053 --> 00:16:12.760
- It was about 30 centimeters
in width and height,

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:13.593
and I just got stuck.

00:16:13.593 --> 00:16:15.320
- Torii like the red shrine
things you see around?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.689
- Yeah, this one was made of concrete.

00:16:16.689 --> 00:16:18.783
It's like concreted into the ground,

