I'm a big boy, I can decide not to eat it.

00:31:36.470 --> 00:31:37.303
Because, right,

00:31:37.303 --> 00:31:40.110
it's like rice, like a
shit ton of miso soup,

00:31:40.110 --> 00:31:42.382
fish, a bunch of other shit that turns up.

00:31:42.382 --> 00:31:43.360
- I can do the miso soup,

00:31:43.360 --> 00:31:45.468
'cause that's like nice
on the stomach, right?

00:31:45.468 --> 00:31:46.607
Miso soup and tofu, I'm like,

00:31:46.607 --> 00:31:50.370
that's nice on the stomach
so I can eat that all night.

00:31:50.370 --> 00:31:51.330
Yeah, fish maybe.

00:31:51.330 --> 00:31:52.410
- Fish is dependent.

00:31:52.410 --> 00:31:53.408
- Fish is maybe, yeah.

00:31:53.408 --> 00:31:56.730
- Because I don't eat
breakfast a lot normally,

00:31:56.730 --> 00:32:00.140
so a Japanese breakfast is
like a five course meal,

00:32:00.140 --> 00:32:01.310
or something like that.

00:32:01.310 --> 00:32:03.100
And this is more than I have for lunch,

00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:04.430
let alone a fucking breakfast.

00:32:04.430 --> 00:32:05.650
- Yeah, it's like a breakfast you give

00:32:05.650 --> 00:32:07.140
to someone who hasn't eaten in three days,

00:32:07.140 --> 00:32:07.973
you know?

00:32:07.973 --> 00:32:09.270
It's a shit load of food.

00:32:09.270 --> 00:32:10.590
- I mean, you dine like a king,

00:32:10.590 --> 00:32:13.330
but at the same time a
king isn't even that hungry

00:32:13.330 --> 00:32:14.970
when he wakes up first
thing in the morning.

00:32:14.970 --> 00:32:16.312
I don't fucking know.

00:32:16.312 --> 00:32:18.220
- Even the king's like,
chill the fuck out bro.

00:32:18.220 --> 00:32:19.898
- Henry the Eighth or something.

00:32:19.898 --> 00:32:21.230
When you're fucking morbidly obese,

00:32:21.230 --> 00:32:23.300
and that's how you start your day.

00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:24.393
It's ridiculous and, you know,

00:32:24.393 --> 00:32:27.070
at the end of the day,
if you're a customer,

00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:27.903
I'm like, you know what?

00:32:27.903 --> 00:32:28.789
I don't need to eat this.

00:32:28.789 --> 00:32:29.970
I don't want to.

00:32:29.970 --> 00:32:30.803
- Oh yeah, I mean,

00:32:30.803 --> 00:32:32.173
you know, if you paid for
it then it's your choice.

00:32:32.173 --> 00:32:33.490
At the end of the day.

00:32:33.490 --> 00:32:34.597
- It's not like I called them up,

00:32:34.597 --> 00:32:35.960
I'm like, bring the breakfast.

00:32:35.960 --> 00:32:37.030
It gets here, it's shit,

00:32:37.030 --> 00:32:37.863
I don't want it.

00:32:37.863 --> 00:32:39.250
It's like it's coming no matter what.

00:32:39.250 --> 00:32:42.090
They're making it
regardless and, you know.

00:32:42.090 --> 00:32:44.730
- 'Cause with most places
breakfast is optional,

00:32:44.730 --> 00:32:47.060
but with a Ryokan, it's
just part of the package,

00:32:47.060 --> 00:32:48.660
and you have no choice to not have--

00:32:48.660 --> 00:32:49.497
- A lot of the times it is, yeah.

00:32:49.497 --> 00:32:51.430
- I can eat a lot as well, right?

00:32:51.430 --> 00:32:54.874
I feel like I could eat a lot,
but these things are massive.

00:32:54.874 --> 00:32:56.280
If you were, you know,

00:32:56.280 --> 00:32:57.133
a smaller person who doesn't eat much,

00:32:57.133 --> 00:32:58.900
there's no way you could finish it.

00:32:58.900 --> 00:33:00.230
- That's why I'm always surprised

00:33:00.230 --> 00:33:01.730
with the amount of food that arrives.

00:33:01.730 --> 00:33:02.563
And I'm like,

00:33:02.563 --> 00:33:04.600
how does an 80 year old Japanese woman

00:33:04.600 --> 00:33:06.790
get up in the morning and eat all of that?

00:33:06.790 --> 00:33:08.390
- I know, right?
- Like how?

00:33:08.390 --> 00:33:11.430
- You just take one bite of
everything and fucking leave it.

00:33:11.430 --> 00:33:12.433
- I mean, it's great for
the first experience,

00:33:12.433 --> 00:33:13.430
because you're like,

00:33:13.430 --> 00:33:15.000
man, this looks fucking amazing.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:16.610
It's like an Instagram meal.

00:33:16.610 --> 00:33:18.250
You take a picture, looks amazing,

00:33:18.250 --> 00:33:19.150
post that, and then you're like,

00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:20.649
fuck, I've got to actually eat this now.

00:33:20.649 --> 00:33:23.433
Fuck, I didn't think about that.

00:33:23.433 --> 00:33:24.940
- It's just not sus.

00:33:24.940 --> 00:33:25.773
I mean, coming from the UK,

00:33:25.773 --> 00:33:28.610
we have a big plate of
everything for breakfast.

00:33:28.610 --> 00:33:30.520
Like I miss British fry ups

00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:31.507
more than anything about the UK.

00:33:31.507 --> 00:33:33.350
- See, I can't even do those either,

00:33:33.350 --> 00:33:35.120
because it's like I just don't wake up

00:33:35.120 --> 00:33:36.320
in the morning and feel hungry.

00:33:36.320 --> 00:33:37.530
- It's more of a lunch thing really.

00:33:37.530 --> 00:33:38.363
- It's a brunch--

00:33:38.363 --> 00:33:39.550
- Yeah, brunch I can do.

00:33:39.550 --> 00:33:41.250
- You kind of eat it at 12:00, 1:00,

00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:43.420
after you've had a heavy night.

00:33:43.420 --> 00:33:44.960
- Have you guys ever had a good

00:33:44.960 --> 00:33:47.200
British kind of fry up in Japan?

00:33:47.200 --> 00:33:48.350
- No.
- Not in Japan, no.

00:33:48.350 --> 00:33:49.300
- I've still not found
anywhere that does it.

00:33:49.300 --> 00:33:51.460
I found fish and chips, woohoo.

00:33:51.460 --> 00:33:53.840
But that's the one thing I can't find.

00:33:53.840 --> 00:33:55.178
- You've found good fish and chips?

00:33:55.178 --> 00:33:56.584
- I have found good fish and chips.

00:33:56.584 --> 00:33:57.800
- Fish and chips is so boring.

00:33:57.800 --> 00:33:58.633
- It is.

00:33:58.633 --> 00:33:59.466
- The English breakfast.

00:33:59.466 --> 00:34:00.577
- The one at Hobgoblin, right?

00:34:00.577 --> 00:34:01.960
- Hobgoblin in Shabu.

00:34:01.960 --> 00:34:02.793
- It's all right.

00:34:02.793 --> 00:34:03.990
- That's probably the best one I've had.

00:34:03.990 --> 00:34:04.880
- It's pretty good, it's pretty good.

00:34:04.880 --> 00:34:06.369
- Really?
- Yeah!

00:34:06.369 --> 00:34:10.236
- But I'm never craving
fish and chips, you know?

00:34:10.236 --> 00:34:11.570
- No, I'm not either.

00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:12.403
I'm not either.

00:34:12.403 --> 00:34:14.607
- You've got some of the best
fish dishes here in Japan,

00:34:14.607 --> 00:34:15.977
and you look at that, you're like,

00:34:15.977 --> 00:34:16.810
you know what?

00:34:16.810 --> 00:34:17.643
Fuck this.

00:34:17.643 --> 00:34:18.960
Fish and chips.

00:34:18.960 --> 00:34:20.182
- I feel like I'm expected to eat it

00:34:20.182 --> 00:34:22.330
because all my years here, right?

00:34:22.330 --> 00:34:23.163
Whenever I go, oh yeah,

00:34:23.163 --> 00:34:24.853
I'm from the UK, one of three things,

00:34:24.853 --> 00:34:26.321
it's like, oh yeah,

00:34:26.321 --> 00:34:29.700
David Bowie, or the Spice Girls,

00:34:29.700 --> 00:34:30.890
fish and chips.

00:34:30.890 --> 00:34:32.700
It's like one of the few
things about British culture,

00:34:32.700 --> 00:34:34.090
so I've kind of like,

00:34:34.090 --> 00:34:34.923
I should probably enjoy fish and chips.

00:34:34.923 --> 00:34:35.756
- Is there anything else?

00:34:35.756 --> 00:34:37.760
- What?
- Like, British cuisine?

00:34:37.760 --> 00:34:39.960
- We have a crisp sandwich.

00:34:39.960 --> 00:34:41.700
- Baked beans.
- Bread sandwich.

00:34:41.700 --> 00:34:42.980
- Sunday roasts.

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:44.300
- Oh, Sunday roast.

00:34:44.300 --> 00:34:45.710
Is there a Sunday roast place in Japan?

00:34:45.710 --> 00:34:47.473
- Yes, Hobgoblin.
- Oh really?

00:34:47.473 --> 00:34:49.410
- Is it good, is it good?

00:34:49.410 --> 00:34:50.310
- It is good.

00:34:50.310 --> 00:34:52.730
- Basically just go to
Hobgoblin apparently.

00:34:52.730 --> 00:34:53.840
- You'll probably bump into us there,

00:34:53.840 --> 00:34:54.673
'cause we go there quite a lot.

00:34:54.673 --> 00:34:55.506
- Yeah, we go there quite a lot.

00:34:55.506 --> 00:34:56.446
Yeah.

00:34:56.446 --> 00:34:57.279
- Genuinely.

00:34:57.279 --> 00:35:00.160
But yeah, British food's hard
to come by unfortunately.

00:35:00.160 --> 00:35:01.910
Sausage rolls, Greggs.

00:35:01.910 --> 00:35:03.110
- I do miss Greggs actually.

00:35:03.110 --> 00:35:04.060
- If it's a franchise,

00:35:04.060 --> 00:35:06.340
couldn't you just buy
one and bring it here?

00:35:06.340 --> 00:35:07.187
- Don't think so--

00:35:07.187 --> 00:35:08.480
- You could be the first,
Trash Taste Greggs.

00:35:08.480 --> 00:35:09.922
- The rules are different, aren't they?

00:35:09.922 --> 00:35:11.030
So it's not--

00:35:11.030 --> 00:35:11.863
- Oh what, like open a Greggs?

00:35:11.863 --> 00:35:12.696
- Yeah!

00:35:12.696 --> 00:35:13.529
Trash Taste Greggs club.

00:35:13.529 --> 00:35:15.220
- It's also not Greggs
unless it's one pound.

00:35:15.220 --> 00:35:16.380
It has to be cheap as fuck.

00:35:16.380 --> 00:35:17.213
If a Greggs is five quid--

00:35:17.213 --> 00:35:18.670
- You could make it 100 Yen, right?

00:35:18.670 --> 00:35:20.798
- There's no way you
could get the costs there.

00:35:20.798 --> 00:35:21.631
- Do it.

00:35:21.631 --> 00:35:23.770
- Oh my God--
- Trash Taste Greggs club.

00:35:23.770 --> 00:35:25.448
- You fucking do it, I'm not doing it.

00:35:25.448 --> 00:35:26.820
(laughs loudly)

00:35:26.820 --> 00:35:28.150
- It's effort.

00:35:28.150 --> 00:35:28.983
- Why should I do it?

00:35:28.983 --> 00:35:31.012
- You've got a studio
the size of Spain, right?

00:35:31.012 --> 00:35:32.670
You could get a Greggs to Japan.

00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:33.760
- That's how you make your first mil.

00:35:33.760 --> 00:35:35.873
Bringing Greggs over to Japan.

00:35:35.873 --> 00:35:37.017
- You could do it.

00:35:37.017 --> 00:35:38.763
- Selling sausage rolls.

00:35:39.602 --> 00:35:41.290
- Anything else that
you miss about England,

00:35:41.290 --> 00:35:44.310
that you crave?

00:35:44.310 --> 00:35:45.143
- Boris Johnson.

00:35:45.143 --> 00:35:46.782
- Boris Johnson--
- Fuck off.

00:35:46.782 --> 00:35:48.506
(laughs loudly)

00:35:48.506 --> 00:35:49.339
Fuck off.

00:35:49.339 --> 00:35:51.810
- And here comes all the dislikes.

00:35:51.810 --> 00:35:53.775
- Finally, you can be in
my corner in this one,

00:35:53.775 --> 00:35:54.963
'cause I've had arguments
with them where--

00:35:54.963 --> 00:35:56.560
- This is always a slippery slope when

00:35:56.560 --> 00:35:58.930
Connor tries to get you
onside about anything.

00:35:58.930 --> 00:36:00.730
- Well, I have to argue with these boys,

00:36:00.730 --> 00:36:02.540
'cause they're like, Tokyo
architecture is amazing.

00:36:02.540 --> 00:36:04.120
I know that you are with me where

00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:05.370
you think London is just beautiful.

00:36:05.370 --> 00:36:06.760
Like, the architecture is amazing.

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:08.090
- It is objectively.

00:36:08.090 --> 00:36:08.963
- And these boys are like, no,

00:36:08.963 --> 00:36:09.796
it's boring, it's boring.

00:36:09.796 --> 00:36:11.120
It's all the same.

00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:12.460
- Well, I mean look at this district here.

00:36:12.460 --> 00:36:13.650
Look out the window, you know?

00:36:13.650 --> 00:36:15.420
There's no interesting
architectural buildings.

00:36:15.420 --> 00:36:16.550
I kind of like the feel of Japan.

00:36:16.550 --> 00:36:18.350
It feels like one big theme park

00:36:18.350 --> 00:36:19.900
'cause everything's kind of clean,

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:21.610
the building's made out of some

00:36:21.610 --> 00:36:23.890
weird woody plastic material.

00:36:23.890 --> 00:36:25.450
It just feels like a theme park almost?

00:36:25.450 --> 00:36:26.283
- But it looks ugly.

00:36:26.283 --> 00:36:27.817
- It looks great, it looks great!

00:36:27.817 --> 00:36:30.360
Japan is literally one of the most

00:36:30.360 --> 00:36:33.200
aesthetic countries in the fucking world.

00:36:33.200 --> 00:36:34.440
- All those areas look really cool,

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.450
but when you start going
10 minutes out of center,

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:37.290
it all just starts to look like

00:36:37.290 --> 00:36:38.440
an amalgamation of just shit--

00:36:38.440 --> 00:36:40.089
- Doesn't every country
look like that though?

00:36:40.089 --> 00:36:41.034
- No, no!

00:36:41.034 --> 00:36:43.186
- You go to fucking Croydon,

00:36:43.186 --> 00:36:44.543
I beg to differ, sir.

00:36:45.945 --> 00:36:47.141
- Every country,

00:36:47.141 --> 00:36:48.630
you go 10 minutes out of the city

00:36:48.630 --> 00:36:50.080
center and it all looks the same.

00:36:50.080 --> 00:36:51.390
- In the UK, the highs are very high,

00:36:51.390 --> 00:36:52.683
and the lows are very low.

00:36:52.683 --> 00:36:54.064
And low is Croydon.

00:36:54.064 --> 00:36:55.140
(laughs loudly)

00:36:55.140 --> 00:36:55.973
In terms of design.

00:36:55.973 --> 00:36:56.950
It's a lovely place, the people are great,

00:36:56.950 --> 00:36:57.816
I love Croydon, but.

00:36:57.816 --> 00:36:58.956
- Shout out to Croydon.

00:36:58.956 --> 00:37:01.874
- Chris, not Croydon's biggest adversary.

00:37:01.874 --> 00:37:03.970
- Jokingly, before Natsky came to the UK,

00:37:03.970 --> 00:37:05.091
I said, where do you want
to go in UK the most?

00:37:05.091 --> 00:37:06.299
He went, Croydon.

00:37:06.299 --> 00:37:08.048
I was like, how do you
even know what that is?

00:37:08.048 --> 00:37:09.261
How do you know what Croydon is?

00:37:09.261 --> 00:37:11.450
- How does he want to
go to one of the most

00:37:11.450 --> 00:37:13.523
depressing places I've
possibly been to in my life?

00:37:13.523 --> 00:37:14.356
- He's still yet to go.

00:37:14.356 --> 00:37:15.860
- Why does he want to go Croydon?

00:37:15.860 --> 00:37:16.850
- Now you have to take him to Croydon.

00:37:16.850 --> 00:37:17.683
- I don't know!

00:37:17.683 --> 00:37:18.516
- How did he learn about
that, who told him?

00:37:18.516 --> 00:37:19.349
- There must have been a band that

00:37:19.349 --> 00:37:21.490
he likes from there or something?

00:37:21.490 --> 00:37:23.690
- Or he heard it from you maybe one time,

00:37:23.690 --> 00:37:25.133
and he was like, that sounds like a place.

00:37:25.133 --> 00:37:27.898
- I don't sit in North
Japan talking about Croydon.

00:37:27.898 --> 00:37:28.931
(Joey laughing loudly)

00:37:28.931 --> 00:37:31.370
Yeah, I don't know where he got it from.

00:37:31.370 --> 00:37:33.740
But no, I'd say the architecture of Japan,

00:37:33.740 --> 00:37:35.670
unfortunately Japan is losing a lot

00:37:35.670 --> 00:37:37.020
of it's old kind of historic buildings.

00:37:37.020 --> 00:37:38.430
Harajuku Station,

00:37:38.430 --> 00:37:41.549
Nakagin Capsule building
is going next year,

00:37:41.549 --> 00:37:44.580
the cool SEGA building
and arcade in Akihabara.

00:37:44.580 --> 00:37:46.600
They've got a very
utilitarian mindset here,

00:37:46.600 --> 00:37:48.410
and Connor's choking to death right now.

00:37:48.410 --> 00:37:49.410
- Jesus.

00:37:49.410 --> 00:37:51.477
- He's gone, time to
take over his channel.

00:37:51.477 --> 00:37:52.310
But like, yeah,

00:37:52.310 --> 00:37:54.420
they've got a very utilitarian mindset.

00:37:54.420 --> 00:37:56.267
As long as it gets the job
done, that's the main thing.

00:37:56.267 --> 00:37:58.900
And if you go to somewhere
like Tokyo Station,

00:37:58.900 --> 00:38:00.620
all the skyscrapers look the same.

00:38:00.620 --> 00:38:01.500
They're all kind off generic.

00:38:01.500 --> 00:38:02.333
- I mean, yeah,

00:38:02.333 --> 00:38:04.040
that part of Japan, or Tokyo,

00:38:04.040 --> 00:38:05.509
is quite bland and gray.

00:38:05.509 --> 00:38:07.570
- And you could go to
any town across Japan,

00:38:07.570 --> 00:38:08.910
it looks more or less the same.

00:38:08.910 --> 00:38:09.887
You'll have the same things.

00:38:09.887 --> 00:38:13.290
It's rare to find good
historic architecture.

00:38:13.290 --> 00:38:15.390
- I don't think it's about the
historic architecture though.

00:38:15.390 --> 00:38:16.223
- No.

00:38:16.223 --> 00:38:17.435
- I like that though.

00:38:17.435 --> 00:38:18.383
- It is cool.

00:38:18.383 --> 00:38:20.210
The historical architecture
in Japan is cool,

00:38:20.210 --> 00:38:22.270
but I think as well they're made, like,

00:38:22.270 --> 00:38:23.533
I think the aesthetic that a lot of people

00:38:23.533 --> 00:38:26.725
love about Japan is
kind of the alleyways--

00:38:26.725 --> 00:38:29.380
- Yeah, Shinjuku grunge.

00:38:29.380 --> 00:38:30.213
Golden Gai looks awesome.

00:38:30.213 --> 00:38:31.853
- Golden Gai looks like it came out

00:38:31.853 --> 00:38:33.120
of a fucking cyberpunk or something.

00:38:33.120 --> 00:38:34.663
That looks amazing.

00:38:35.780 --> 00:38:36.613
Nakameguro?

00:38:36.613 --> 00:38:38.505
Fucking amazing area.

00:38:38.505 --> 00:38:39.690
- But everywhere else
is just so depressing.

00:38:39.690 --> 00:38:40.824
It all just looks like a mess.

00:38:40.824 --> 00:38:43.870
- I kind of think London
is like that, most of it.

00:38:43.870 --> 00:38:45.860
If it's not zone one or zone two

00:38:45.860 --> 00:38:47.510
then what have we got really?

00:38:47.510 --> 00:38:48.840
- London looks really good, I think.

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:50.177
All the buildings look like, I don't know,

00:38:50.177 --> 00:38:51.010
I really like the look.

00:38:51.010 --> 00:38:54.000
It's really nice, really well designed.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:55.076
- 'Cause you lived in Morden.

00:38:55.076 --> 00:38:57.258
What's there in Morden?

00:38:57.258 --> 00:38:58.287
I lived in Streatham.

00:38:58.287 --> 00:39:00.837
Streatham was fucking depressing as shit.

00:39:00.837 --> 00:39:02.180
- Morden just sounds like a fucking

00:39:02.180 --> 00:39:03.628
'Lord Of The Rings' area.

00:39:03.628 --> 00:39:05.960
- It sounds a lot cooler than it looks.

00:39:05.960 --> 00:39:07.780
- We're going to Morden!

00:39:07.780 --> 00:39:08.613
- It looked pretty nice.

00:39:08.613 --> 00:39:09.446
I like it actually.

00:39:09.446 --> 00:39:10.330
