00:58:17.510 --> 00:58:20.260
just sort of far away enough from it,

00:58:20.260 --> 00:58:22.230
but it used to be an island, Sakurajima,

00:58:22.230 --> 00:58:24.758
and then it erupted
and became a peninsula,

00:58:24.758 --> 00:58:25.980
because the lava just connected with

00:58:25.980 --> 00:58:27.210
the land and built a land bridge,

00:58:27.210 --> 00:58:30.200
so it's a pretty hardcore volcano.

00:58:30.200 --> 00:58:32.650
Too much volcano, some would say.

00:58:32.650 --> 00:58:34.061
- It's not Krakatoa though, is it?

00:58:34.061 --> 00:58:34.894
- It's no Krakatoa--

00:58:34.894 --> 00:58:36.008
- It's no Krakatoa!

00:58:36.008 --> 00:58:36.841
(laughs loudly)

00:58:36.841 --> 00:58:39.740
- It's no Krakatoa, it
sounds like a game show.

00:58:39.740 --> 00:58:40.810
Is it Krakatoa?

00:58:40.810 --> 00:58:43.240
- Why are you obsessed
with fucking Krakatoa?

00:58:43.240 --> 00:58:45.081
- It just sounds cool.

00:58:45.081 --> 00:58:45.920
It's a cool sounding volcano.

00:58:45.920 --> 00:58:47.110
- Krakatoa.

00:58:47.110 --> 00:58:49.300
- Yeah, because you always seem to find

00:58:49.300 --> 00:58:51.260
some really out there ideas,

00:58:51.260 --> 00:58:53.440
cool ideas for not just
Journey Across Japan,

00:58:53.440 --> 00:58:54.407
but just in general,

00:58:54.407 --> 00:58:56.520
and these guys were talking
about how you literally

00:58:56.520 --> 00:58:58.590
fucking scour Google maps or something.

00:58:58.590 --> 00:58:59.423
- Yeah, I mean--

00:58:59.423 --> 00:59:00.256
- What goes into that?

00:59:00.256 --> 00:59:01.460
- There's definitely variables
in Journey Across Japan,

00:59:01.460 --> 00:59:03.403
like, we have a kind
of start and end place.

00:59:03.403 --> 00:59:06.025
We have the hotel at the
beginning and the end,

00:59:06.025 --> 00:59:07.800
and then I have a few locations lined up,

00:59:07.800 --> 00:59:09.600
and then I sort of keep it from,

00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:11.850
in this season I kept
it from Joey and Natsky.

00:59:11.850 --> 00:59:12.683
Then we get challenges,

00:59:12.683 --> 00:59:14.980
and then the challenges
shape what happens, right.

00:59:14.980 --> 00:59:16.660
So the day we did the
rap 'Too Much Volcano',

00:59:16.660 --> 00:59:17.772
we could have done anything.

00:59:17.772 --> 00:59:20.050
Could have been like eat
the worst food in Kyoto,

00:59:20.050 --> 00:59:20.883
or, you know,

00:59:20.883 --> 00:59:21.716
something like that.

00:59:21.716 --> 00:59:22.549
So there's lots of variables that

00:59:22.549 --> 00:59:23.960
keeps it fresh and original.

00:59:23.960 --> 00:59:26.490
But when you've got a
team of like five people,

00:59:26.490 --> 00:59:27.540
and, you know,

00:59:27.540 --> 00:59:30.110
it's a very pricey experience to make,

00:59:30.110 --> 00:59:31.390
you've got to make sure that you're

00:59:31.390 --> 00:59:32.530
actually doing good things, right?

00:59:32.530 --> 00:59:33.363
You know?

00:59:33.363 --> 00:59:35.290
So the various places are planned out,

00:59:35.290 --> 00:59:37.400
but I wouldn't say it's scripted as such.

00:59:37.400 --> 00:59:38.233
- No, no,
no.

00:59:38.233 --> 00:59:39.840
I feel Journey Across Japan 3 though

00:59:39.840 --> 00:59:42.210
was like way more intense than two.

00:59:42.210 --> 00:59:45.520
Like I feel, I just feel like
that week of three was just,

00:59:45.520 --> 00:59:46.620
we did, I reckon,

00:59:46.620 --> 00:59:48.810
twice as much stuff as we did in two.

00:59:48.810 --> 00:59:49.743
At least that's what it felt like to me.

00:59:49.743 --> 00:59:50.710
- Just asked myself,

00:59:50.710 --> 00:59:53.020
how could you make the
ultimate series in a week?

00:59:53.020 --> 00:59:55.150
And that's pretty much, all
the stuff I found led to that.

00:59:55.150 --> 00:59:57.220
- So how long did it take in total?

00:59:57.220 --> 00:59:59.090
- To find all those places?

00:59:59.090 --> 01:00:00.463
- Or to like plan it out, schedule it,

01:00:00.463 --> 01:00:01.662
and all that?

01:00:01.662 --> 01:00:03.373
- I don't know, three days?

01:00:03.373 --> 01:00:04.340
- Three days?

01:00:04.340 --> 01:00:06.070
- 72 hours.
- No fucking way--

01:00:06.070 --> 01:00:07.400
- I did actually spend two or

01:00:07.400 --> 01:00:08.380
three days just glued to Google,

01:00:08.380 --> 01:00:09.356
like, fucking,

01:00:09.356 --> 01:00:10.189
what is there?

01:00:10.189 --> 01:00:11.650
- I spend more time trying
to spend my fucking holiday.

01:00:11.650 --> 01:00:15.080
You just planned an
entire fucking special,

01:00:15.080 --> 01:00:16.430
like a five day special.

01:00:16.430 --> 01:00:17.880
- I think that the greatest find was this

01:00:17.880 --> 01:00:19.750
abandoned island called Ikashima.

01:00:19.750 --> 01:00:20.701
There's like a,

01:00:20.701 --> 01:00:22.410
the abandoned island everyone knows

01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:23.650
near Nagasaki is Gunkanjima,

01:00:23.650 --> 01:00:24.580
battleship island,

01:00:24.580 --> 01:00:25.843
which you've probably seen in 'Skyfall'--

01:00:25.843 --> 01:00:26.842
- Terrible though.
- What?

01:00:26.842 --> 01:00:28.210
- Because you can't
fucking do anything there.

01:00:28.210 --> 01:00:29.360
- Well, yeah!

01:00:29.360 --> 01:00:31.240
I thought you could walk
around it but you can only go--

01:00:31.240 --> 01:00:32.940
- 90% of it is blocked off.

01:00:32.940 --> 01:00:33.850
- So we could only go as a tour,

01:00:33.850 --> 01:00:35.500
and that was going to be the
centerpiece of this series.

01:00:35.500 --> 01:00:36.464
So once I discovered that,

01:00:36.464 --> 01:00:37.297
I was like, we're fucked.

01:00:37.297 --> 01:00:38.580
And I got really depressed,

01:00:38.580 --> 01:00:40.640
and I was like, is it even
worth doing this series now?

01:00:40.640 --> 01:00:41.650
The lost islands?

01:00:41.650 --> 01:00:42.714
It's not gonna work, is it?

01:00:42.714 --> 01:00:44.810
It's just going to be the boring islands.

01:00:44.810 --> 01:00:46.720
So I kept looking around Nagasaki,

01:00:46.720 --> 01:00:49.650
and I found just 40 kilometers
north another island.

01:00:49.650 --> 01:00:51.908
Bigger, 10 times bigger than Gunkanjima,

01:00:51.908 --> 01:00:53.560
30 abandoned buildings,

01:00:53.560 --> 01:00:54.950
like a city, a mini city--

01:00:54.950 --> 01:00:57.160
- And less than 100 people live there.

01:00:57.160 --> 01:00:57.993
- Yeah, 100 or so people live there

01:00:57.993 --> 01:00:59.655
and you can explore it freely.

01:00:59.655 --> 01:01:00.488
- It looked really cool

01:01:00.488 --> 01:01:01.321
- It did look really cool,

01:01:01.321 --> 01:01:02.170
and that was my, kind of,

01:01:02.170 --> 01:01:03.460
probably my favorite episode actually.

01:01:03.460 --> 01:01:05.480
- So what what's your process
of finding these places?

01:01:05.480 --> 01:01:06.530
'Cause I would like to know,

01:01:06.530 --> 01:01:08.500
because I, you know,

01:01:08.500 --> 01:01:10.550
I would like to travel
around more around Japan,

01:01:10.550 --> 01:01:12.380
but I literally don't know
where to fucking start.

01:01:12.380 --> 01:01:15.307
Like you do a Google search
about cool places to go in Japan

01:01:15.307 --> 01:01:16.999
and you get the same 10 articles.

01:01:16.999 --> 01:01:18.060
- Shinjuku, Shibuya!

01:01:18.060 --> 01:01:18.893
- Yeah, you get the same 10

01:01:18.893 --> 01:01:21.165
articles with the same 20 places.

01:01:21.165 --> 01:01:21.998
- Kyoto!

01:01:21.998 --> 01:01:22.987
- In every fucking article.

01:01:22.987 --> 01:01:23.820
- Surely you just pick a place,

01:01:23.820 --> 01:01:24.976
like a place you want to go to,

01:01:24.976 --> 01:01:25.809
and then you start looking at

01:01:25.809 --> 01:01:27.118
everything around the area, right?

01:01:27.118 --> 01:01:28.440
- Well, switch to Japanese.

01:01:28.440 --> 01:01:30.610
Use Japanese to search,
it gets a lot easier,

01:01:30.610 --> 01:01:31.580
because obviously the people that know

01:01:31.580 --> 01:01:32.710
the places are going to be in Japan,

01:01:32.710 --> 01:01:33.760
speak Japanese.

01:01:33.760 --> 01:01:35.570
And so if you do that, you'll find like

01:01:35.570 --> 01:01:37.040
10 times more interesting places.

01:01:37.040 --> 01:01:38.895
Otherwise it's just the
way, it's tourist hotspots.

01:01:38.895 --> 01:01:40.161
That's my advice.

01:01:40.161 --> 01:01:43.300
Get someone who can speak
Japanese to look up these places.

01:01:43.300 --> 01:01:44.680
Yeah.

01:01:44.680 --> 01:01:45.513
Mailin, great.

01:01:46.860 --> 01:01:47.693
Or him.

01:01:47.693 --> 01:01:49.940
- Now to just find that Japanese person.

01:01:49.940 --> 01:01:50.773
- Joey?

01:01:50.773 --> 01:01:51.606
(laughs loudly)

01:01:51.606 --> 01:01:53.308
Joey planning the next
Trash Taste special?

01:01:53.308 --> 01:01:54.783
- Yeah, sure.

01:01:55.740 --> 01:01:56.573
I guess.

