- I just find it hilarious.

01:18:31.421 --> 01:18:33.320
I can't think of a more
British thing than trying

01:18:33.320 --> 01:18:36.858
to climb Mount Fuji with
shorts and a T-shirt, right?

01:18:36.858 --> 01:18:37.691
- It's pretty Brit.

01:18:37.691 --> 01:18:40.300
- It's 'cause it's just
like (laughs loudly),

01:18:40.300 --> 01:18:41.930
like in England, you see sunshine,

01:18:41.930 --> 01:18:42.763
and it's just like, all right,

01:18:42.763 --> 01:18:43.596
it could be, like,

01:18:43.596 --> 01:18:45.150
15, 16 degrees.

01:18:45.150 --> 01:18:45.983
You see a bit of sun,

01:18:45.983 --> 01:18:47.280
shorts and T-shirts time, right?

01:18:47.280 --> 01:18:48.180
- It's hard though, to imagine,

01:18:48.180 --> 01:18:50.160
like when you're staying
outside, 36 degrees,

01:18:50.160 --> 01:18:52.030
it's hard to think there's
nowhere in this country that

01:18:52.030 --> 01:18:54.541
could be cold enough to need
something like that, right?

01:18:54.541 --> 01:18:55.374
So, you know,

01:18:55.374 --> 01:18:57.153
you go from Central Tokyo, Shinjuku,

01:18:57.153 --> 01:18:57.986
where we started,

01:18:57.986 --> 01:19:00.000
to Mount Fuji, two hour bus rides,

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:01.000
and then, bang--

01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:02.990
- Did you not just think maybe
I should just give a quick

01:19:02.990 --> 01:19:05.293
Google as to what goes on on Mount Fuji?

01:19:05.293 --> 01:19:06.823
- Maybe I should check the weather?

01:19:06.823 --> 01:19:07.656
- Yeah, see what goes on.

01:19:07.656 --> 01:19:08.862
You know, what do people recommend doing?

01:19:08.862 --> 01:19:11.956
- I did have a ski jacket and shorts.

01:19:11.956 --> 01:19:13.450
My friend went in just T-shirt--

01:19:13.450 --> 01:19:15.043
- And you didn't tell your friend?

01:19:15.043 --> 01:19:15.900
- I did, I did!

01:19:15.900 --> 01:19:17.073
He was like, I'll be all right.

01:19:17.073 --> 01:19:18.090
(laughs loudly)

01:19:18.090 --> 01:19:19.630
- Was he British?
- Oh yeah.

01:19:19.630 --> 01:19:20.463
- Okay, that sounds about right.

01:19:20.463 --> 01:19:21.490
- He was not.

01:19:21.490 --> 01:19:22.323
- I'm surprised you're able to

01:19:22.323 --> 01:19:24.455
sleep in that fucking cold with--

01:19:24.455 --> 01:19:25.288
- We didn't really.

01:19:25.288 --> 01:19:26.510
I remember just hell, just hell.

01:19:26.510 --> 01:19:28.173
- Why did you carry on to the top?

01:19:28.173 --> 01:19:30.430
- 'Cause you're so battered by that point.

01:19:30.430 --> 01:19:31.263
- Fair enough.

01:19:31.263 --> 01:19:32.096
- And you're not supposed to!

01:19:32.096 --> 01:19:33.490
A lot of the clever people do

01:19:33.490 --> 01:19:34.618
something called bullet climbing,

01:19:34.618 --> 01:19:35.750
although it's not really clever.

01:19:35.750 --> 01:19:37.140
When you get to the
base, there's something,

01:19:37.140 --> 01:19:38.653
a sign saying don't bullet climb.

01:19:38.653 --> 01:19:40.530
A bullet climb is where you rush up

01:19:40.530 --> 01:19:41.363
the mountain as quick as you can,

01:19:41.363 --> 01:19:42.310
you know, like five,

01:19:42.310 --> 01:19:44.130
six hours, and you come back down.

01:19:44.130 --> 01:19:46.400
But a lot of people get towards the top,

01:19:46.400 --> 01:19:47.780
the oxygen deprivation kicks in,

01:19:47.780 --> 01:19:50.340
they sort of pass out and get fucked up.

01:19:50.340 --> 01:19:51.660
So you're supposed to do it kind of slowly

01:19:51.660 --> 01:19:54.500
to acclimatize to the lack of oxygen.

01:19:54.500 --> 01:19:56.500
I know a lot of good friends
that do it in one morning.

01:19:56.500 --> 01:19:57.573
Go there, get there the afternoon,

01:19:57.573 --> 01:19:58.406
come back down.

01:19:58.406 --> 01:19:59.510
And I'd probably do that,

01:19:59.510 --> 01:20:01.710
if I was gonna do it again
I'd probably just do that.

01:20:01.710 --> 01:20:03.471
The sunset was great, but it's like--

01:20:03.471 --> 01:20:06.050
- Is finding accomodation
there just a nightmare,

01:20:06.050 --> 01:20:07.030
to stay in?

01:20:07.030 --> 01:20:08.250
- Accommodation?

01:20:08.250 --> 01:20:10.250
Well, it just gets booked up very quick.

01:20:11.619 --> 01:20:12.452
- I heard you've got to know

01:20:12.452 --> 01:20:14.790
people to get accomodation there,

01:20:14.790 --> 01:20:16.307
and I didn't know that the alternative

01:20:16.307 --> 01:20:17.910
was just sleeping on a rock,

01:20:17.910 --> 01:20:19.460
but I guess now I know.

01:20:19.460 --> 01:20:21.466
- Are you allowed to do that?

01:20:21.466 --> 01:20:23.382
Are you allowed to just
sleep on a mountain?

01:20:23.382 --> 01:20:24.215
- You don't get much choice.

01:20:24.215 --> 01:20:25.897
- I don't think it's recommended.

01:20:25.897 --> 01:20:27.670
- It's in the dark, it's
pitch black up there.

01:20:27.670 --> 01:20:28.930
You can't see right.

01:20:28.930 --> 01:20:30.170
I went off the track a little bit,

01:20:30.170 --> 01:20:31.830
and just found a volcanic rock,

01:20:31.830 --> 01:20:34.174
slept on it, job done.

01:20:34.174 --> 01:20:36.450
(laughing quickly)

01:20:36.450 --> 01:20:38.892
- It's volcanic, it's kind of warm?

01:20:38.892 --> 01:20:39.930
- Laughing at me for my lack of

01:20:39.930 --> 01:20:41.520
sports when I've slept on a rock.

01:20:41.520 --> 01:20:43.030
- Straight from Krakatoa, this rock.

01:20:43.030 --> 01:20:44.186
- Straight from Krakatoa.

01:20:44.186 --> 01:20:46.200
- I'm not going to be
impressed by your stupidity.

01:20:46.200 --> 01:20:47.800
Why would I be impressed by that?

01:20:47.800 --> 01:20:49.140
- You just wait until I climb Krakatoa.

01:20:49.140 --> 01:20:50.790
We'll see who has the last laugh.

01:20:52.480 --> 01:20:53.843
- You're gonna climb anything.

01:20:55.079 --> 01:20:56.409
- I don't even know how tall it is.

01:20:56.409 --> 01:20:57.810
- It's probably very tall.

01:20:57.810 --> 01:20:59.914
- Something else to find out.

01:20:59.914 --> 01:21:01.240
- I think it's like the biggest

01:21:01.240 --> 01:21:02.890
volcano in the world right now,

01:21:02.890 --> 01:21:03.723
I don't know--

01:21:04.678 --> 01:21:05.511
- Top 10 volcanoes.

01:21:05.511 --> 01:21:06.810
- What, Krakatoa?
- Krakatoa.

01:21:06.810 --> 01:21:08.060
- Is it?
- I think so.

01:21:08.060 --> 01:21:08.970
It's definitely one of the most

01:21:08.970 --> 01:21:10.470
famous volcanoes in the world.

01:21:10.470 --> 01:21:11.394
- I'd never heard of it.

01:21:11.394 --> 01:21:13.080
- What the fuck is
going on with these two?

01:21:13.080 --> 01:21:13.947
- Why are they laughing?

01:21:13.947 --> 01:21:16.460
- Why are we talking about
this fucking volcano?

01:21:16.460 --> 01:21:17.293
Why are we talking about this?

01:21:17.293 --> 01:21:18.126
- [Garnt] I don't know.

01:21:18.126 --> 01:21:19.600
Chris just seems to fucking want

01:21:19.600 --> 01:21:21.930
to mention it for some reason--

01:21:21.930 --> 01:21:23.890
- Someone made me a bet, $1000,

01:21:23.890 --> 01:21:25.210
that I could get the world Krakatoa

01:21:25.210 --> 01:21:26.670
said 100 times on Trash Taste.

01:21:26.670 --> 01:21:27.680
- He just wants us to say volcano

01:21:27.680 --> 01:21:29.513
so it promotes his new fucking song.

01:21:29.513 --> 01:21:30.680
- Hey, I'm okay with that.

01:21:30.680 --> 01:21:31.915
I'm in it.

01:21:31.915 --> 01:21:33.593
- 33% of the profit.
- Yeah.

01:21:34.530 --> 01:21:35.920
Go iTunes.

01:21:35.920 --> 01:21:38.232
- Give me 5% and I'll shill it.

01:21:38.232 --> 01:21:40.232
- What, we're gonna fucking sponsor you?

01:21:41.660 --> 01:21:42.493
- Give me the Umeshu.

01:21:42.493 --> 01:21:43.860
- Give me the whole bottle.

01:21:43.860 --> 01:21:46.350
- Sponsored by 'Too Much Volcano'.

01:21:46.350 --> 01:21:48.750
- No, I'm running out of really cool,

01:21:48.750 --> 01:21:50.467
kind of cool things to do in Japan.

01:21:50.467 --> 01:21:52.210
- You've done everything.

01:21:52.210 --> 01:21:53.260
- How many prefectures do you have?

01:21:53.260 --> 01:21:54.093
You said like four, right?

01:21:54.093 --> 01:21:56.384
- I've got two prefectures to go to.

01:21:56.384 --> 01:21:58.655
- Two prefectures, and what are they?

01:21:58.655 --> 01:22:02.640
- Kochi in Shikoku, and Miyazaki,

01:22:02.640 --> 01:22:03.473
which we kind of drove through--

01:22:03.473 --> 01:22:04.960
- We drove through Miyazaki, yeah.

01:22:04.960 --> 01:22:06.844
- I can't, can we call that?

01:22:06.844 --> 01:22:08.482
I'm kind of feeling that we should now.

01:22:08.482 --> 01:22:09.898
But all right.

01:22:09.898 --> 01:22:11.560
So Miyazaki and Kochi, and that's it.

01:22:11.560 --> 01:22:12.417
- Oh wow.

01:22:12.417 --> 01:22:14.700
- And maybe Shimane, so that's three.

01:22:14.700 --> 01:22:17.230
- Do you feel like you've
almost completed Japan?

01:22:17.230 --> 01:22:18.240
- Well, I've got my,

01:22:18.240 --> 01:22:20.033
I've got a scratch map of Japan.

01:22:20.033 --> 01:22:21.560
Course I do, and I scratch,

01:22:21.560 --> 01:22:22.493
every time I go somewhere, I'm like,

01:22:22.493 --> 01:22:23.326
yeah, I've gone to that prefecture.

01:22:23.326 --> 01:22:25.503
And it's got only a few
bits to scratch off now,

01:22:25.503 --> 01:22:27.373
and then I'll be done.

01:22:28.533 --> 01:22:29.440
- What are you gonna do after that?

01:22:29.440 --> 01:22:30.490
- Bits and pieces of Rokunohe.

01:22:30.490 --> 01:22:32.540
The Pacific Islands of
Japan, like Yakushima.

01:22:32.540 --> 01:22:34.995
I don't know if you've ever seen it,

01:22:34.995 --> 01:22:36.410
yeah, it looks like a
proper Bond villain's lair.

01:22:36.410 --> 01:22:37.610
- You're stretching it
thin now, aren't you?

01:22:37.610 --> 01:22:38.760
You're just like, Jesus,

01:22:38.760 --> 01:22:39.593
anything, is there--

01:22:39.593 --> 01:22:40.541
- Give me something.

01:22:40.541 --> 01:22:42.810
- Is there a raccoon
village somewhere, anything.

01:22:42.810 --> 01:22:45.202
- Probably is to be honest--
- It's called Shibuya.

01:22:45.202 --> 01:22:46.960
(all laughing quickly)

01:22:46.960 --> 01:22:47.955
- But yeah, no,

01:22:47.955 --> 01:22:49.710
I feel like I've got to finish up places.

01:22:49.710 --> 01:22:51.997
- You're kind of in the end game now.

01:22:51.997 --> 01:22:53.546
- Start doing soapland reviews I guess.

01:22:53.546 --> 01:22:54.379
- The endgame.

01:22:54.379 --> 01:22:56.400
- It's kind of the endgame.

01:22:56.400 --> 01:22:57.713
- Scratch the last one, just.

01:22:57.713 --> 01:23:00.740
(laughing loudly)

01:23:00.740 --> 01:23:03.700
On the summit of Mount
Fuji, (groaning loudly).

01:23:03.700 --> 01:23:04.533
Fuck, I don't know.

01:23:04.533 --> 01:23:06.770
But there's still lots
of places in prefectures.

01:23:06.770 --> 01:23:08.750
I've only just passed through
some of those prefectures,

01:23:08.750 --> 01:23:10.756
and there's still lots
of things to see and do.

01:23:10.756 --> 01:23:12.180
- Is it getting hard to
find video topics though?

01:23:12.180 --> 01:23:13.259
or do you still feel like
you've got an abundance--

01:23:13.259 --> 01:23:14.906
- No, I feel like there's
still an endless amount.

01:23:14.906 --> 01:23:17.550
Like I've only just made a
video yesterday on Asakusa,

01:23:17.550 --> 01:23:18.560
the district in Tokyo.

01:23:18.560 --> 01:23:19.554
- Really?

01:23:19.554 --> 01:23:20.921
- That most tourists in Japan go to.

01:23:20.921 --> 01:23:23.270
- It's fucking awful when
there's tourists there.

01:23:23.270 --> 01:23:24.887
- It can be, but it's a
beautiful part of town.

01:23:24.887 --> 01:23:26.930
- Takista's fucking horrible
when there's tourists.

01:23:26.930 --> 01:23:28.440
- That's the shrine, right?

01:23:28.440 --> 01:23:29.273
- Harajuku, yeah,

01:23:29.273 --> 01:23:30.106
yeah, Sensoji Temple.

01:23:30.106 --> 01:23:31.000
- You also can't take pictures

01:23:31.000 --> 01:23:32.890
of that and post them online--

01:23:32.890 --> 01:23:34.000
- We were filming,

01:23:34.000 --> 01:23:35.848
and the security guards
sort of wandered up

01:23:35.848 --> 01:23:37.366
and just came into shot behind us,

01:23:37.366 --> 01:23:38.217
and we were like, what's he doing?

01:23:38.217 --> 01:23:39.050
Oh, fuck it,

01:23:39.050 --> 01:23:39.883
we can't film here.

01:23:39.883 --> 01:23:40.860
But luckily we got away with it

01:23:40.860 --> 01:23:42.180
just in time before he turned up.

01:23:42.180 --> 01:23:43.770
- Apparently you get
fined through, I heard?

01:23:43.770 --> 01:23:44.790
- We didn't get fined.

01:23:44.790 --> 01:23:46.732
- If you post it, so we'll see.

01:23:46.732 --> 01:23:50.030
- Bring it on, bring it on Asakusa.

01:23:50.030 --> 01:23:51.940
No, please don't.

01:23:51.940 --> 01:23:52.995
- It's a promotional video!

01:23:52.995 --> 01:23:55.247
- We're trying to promote you
guys, trying to help you out.

01:23:55.247 --> 01:23:56.630
- I don't know why they
would do that though.

01:23:56.630 --> 01:23:57.560
It seems a bit of an odd,

01:23:57.560 --> 01:24:01.237
for such a massive
tourist thing, you know?

01:24:01.237 --> 01:24:03.200
- You don't think there's hundreds

01:24:03.200 --> 01:24:04.470
of tourists taking pictures of it, right?

01:24:04.470 --> 01:24:06.840
- Yeah, because the
Eiffel tower is private

01:24:06.840 --> 01:24:08.416
property that you technically,

01:24:08.416 --> 01:24:10.140
you know, you can't
actually take picture of.

01:24:10.140 --> 01:24:10.973
- [Joey] Really?

01:24:10.973 --> 01:24:14.245
- For a commercial use, but
they do it all the time 'cause--

01:24:14.245 --> 01:24:16.440
- There's nothing stopping them, right?

01:24:16.440 --> 01:24:17.710
- You can't regulate that.

01:24:17.710 --> 01:24:19.430
It's literally in the skyline.

01:24:19.430 --> 01:24:21.110
- Japan is like, bet?

01:24:21.110 --> 01:24:21.943
We're gonna try and regulate it--

01:24:21.943 --> 01:24:22.813
- What's really weird about filming laws,

01:24:22.813 --> 01:24:25.200
like have you ever been
to a Japanese concert?

01:24:25.200 --> 01:24:26.620
Or Japanese music?

01:24:26.620 --> 01:24:28.321
- I've been to a concert but I haven't,

01:24:28.321 --> 01:24:29.682
they don't let you film it, do they?

01:24:29.682 --> 01:24:30.515
- No, no,

01:24:30.515 --> 01:24:31.400
no, they don't let you film it at all.

01:24:31.400 --> 01:24:35.310
- It's really looked down
upon to film a concert,

01:24:35.310 --> 01:24:36.535
a live concert, whereas--

01:24:36.535 --> 01:24:38.484
- I wouldn't mind that, to be honest.

01:24:38.484 --> 01:24:39.740
Just live in the moment, innit?

01:24:39.740 --> 01:24:40.630
- They're pretty good about it, actually.

01:24:40.630 --> 01:24:43.360
- You can't even relive
the moment for yourself.

01:24:43.360 --> 01:24:44.840
- When I did the documentary on Hide,

01:24:44.840 --> 01:24:47.210
the rockstar guy, nobody
took out their phone.

01:24:47.210 --> 01:24:48.043
You can see no one,

01:24:48.043 --> 01:24:49.260
apart from the end when he gets everyone

01:24:49.260 --> 01:24:50.407
out to put their lights on their phone,

01:24:50.407 --> 01:24:52.120
create a sea of light.

01:24:52.120 --> 01:24:53.940
Other than that, they're
pretty damn strict on that.

01:24:53.940 --> 01:24:55.747
- It's so that they--
- I don't mind that though.

01:24:55.747 --> 01:24:57.010
- But the reason they do that is

01:24:57.010 --> 01:24:58.760
so they get you to buy the DVD.

01:24:58.760 --> 01:24:59.984
- Yeah, yeah,
yeah.

01:24:59.984 --> 01:25:00.817
- [Connor] Oh.

01:25:00.817 --> 01:25:01.650
- Right?

01:25:01.650 --> 01:25:02.500
So it's just a promotional tool.

01:25:02.500 --> 01:25:04.390
- I thought it would be
some kind of spiritual jam.

01:25:04.390 --> 01:25:05.719
You have to appreciate the artist.

01:25:05.719 --> 01:25:07.020
- You have to live in the moment!

01:25:07.020 --> 01:25:08.552
- No, just buy our fucking merch.

01:25:08.552 --> 01:25:09.385
Buy our DVD--

01:25:09.385 --> 01:25:10.218
- Yeah, buy our DVD,

01:25:10.218 --> 01:25:11.540
it's literally that.

01:25:11.540 --> 01:25:13.680
- Hide did a credit card,
the Hide credit card.

01:25:13.680 --> 01:25:14.619
- What?

01:25:14.619 --> 01:25:16.160
- As his merchandise, his
merchandise is off the charts.

01:25:16.160 --> 01:25:17.200
- [Connor] What the fuck?

01:25:17.200 --> 01:25:18.970
- He made so much money from
it, I was really impressed.

01:25:18.970 --> 01:25:19.803
- Well, yeah,

01:25:19.803 --> 01:25:20.636
he's selling fucking credit cards.

01:25:20.636 --> 01:25:21.900
- Where's the Abroad in Japan credit card?

01:25:21.900 --> 01:25:24.580
- We've got the top 14 iTunes.

01:25:24.580 --> 01:25:26.110
Take that.

01:25:26.110 --> 01:25:27.960
- Credit card coming soon.

01:25:27.960 --> 01:25:29.430
- Abroad in Japan credit card?

01:25:29.430 --> 01:25:30.263
- Yeah, that's what I want.

01:25:30.263 --> 01:25:31.753
- It would be a shit show.

01:25:33.521 --> 01:25:34.840
What would it do?

01:25:34.840 --> 01:25:36.938
- It's a credit card, what do you mean?

01:25:36.938 --> 01:25:37.902
- It's a credit card!

01:25:37.902 --> 01:25:39.250
- It doesn't do anything,
it's just got your face on it.

01:25:39.250 --> 01:25:40.750
- Perfect.

01:25:40.750 --> 01:25:42.930
- The entire card is just that face.

01:25:42.930 --> 01:25:46.680
- I got approached by a company
once to make a Natsky doll,

01:25:46.680 --> 01:25:47.530
and you'd squeeze it,
and it would be like,

01:25:47.530 --> 01:25:48.536
go fuck yourself.

01:25:48.536 --> 01:25:50.060
(all laughing loudly)

01:25:50.060 --> 01:25:51.200
- Why did you not say yes to that?

01:25:51.200 --> 01:25:52.190
- Sounds like a genius idea.

01:25:52.190 --> 01:25:53.579
- I don't know, I don't know.

01:25:53.579 --> 01:25:55.104
I didn't want to exploit Natsky.

01:25:55.104 --> 01:25:56.220
- I think he wanted the experience--

01:25:56.220 --> 01:25:57.873
- To be fair, I asked him,

01:25:57.873 --> 01:25:58.706
and he's like, yeah,

01:25:58.706 --> 01:25:59.539
why haven't we done it?

01:25:59.539 --> 01:26:00.372
And I'm like, oh shit.

01:26:00.372 --> 01:26:01.397
So I might still do it,
I might still do it.

01:26:01.397 --> 01:26:02.670
- Now you've said it now,

01:26:02.670 --> 01:26:04.012
you're never gonna hear the end of this.

01:26:04.012 --> 01:26:04.930
